cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  DynaMate: a reproducible GROMACS molecular dynamics workflow for
  protein-cofactor-metal-ligand systems
message: If you use DynaMate in your research, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chanda
    given-names: Vishal
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1646-6329
    affiliation: REVA University, Bengaluru, India
repository-code: https://github.com/Vishu1197/DynaMate
url: https://github.com/Vishu1197/DynaMate
abstract: >-
  DynaMate automates the setup, equilibration, production and analysis of
  all-atom molecular dynamics simulations of proteins carrying a cofactor, a
  metal ion and a docked ligand. Protein parameters come from an AMBER force
  field; cofactor and ligand parameters are generated with GAFF2 and AM1-BCC
  charges through AmberTools; the metal ion is taken from the force field's own
  ion parameters. Every molecule is renamed to a generic label (Protein, COF,
  MI, LIG) so that commands, file names and analysis groups are identical
  between projects. The workflow is built around the failure modes of manual
  setup that produce a valid but silently incorrect topology, and checks for
  each of them explicitly.
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - GROMACS
  - AmberTools
  - GAFF2
  - protein-ligand interaction
  - cofactor
  - metal ion
  - computational biology
  - structural bioinformatics
  - MM-PBSA
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
version: '2.0'
date-released: '2026-09-12'
